# analysis-core-v1: the DOCUMENT VIEW (DS022 "Analysis procedures"). The analyzer (lib/analysis/view.mjs) writes these facts for one
# run, deterministically, from the closure of the document layer under the selected procedures' rules: one fact per literal that
# depends on a document wire. They are structure, not understanding: the canonical text of an atom and of a functional value. The view
# is complete by construction (every literal of the closure is written), so its predicates are closed.

@asserted_atom predicate
  args subject:text
  closed true
  label en "asserted atom"
  description "Document view: the atom (canonical SOP text) has positive evidence in the closure of the document layer."

@denied_atom predicate
  args subject:text
  closed true
  label en "denied atom"
  description "Document view: the atom (canonical SOP text) has negative evidence (an explicit not) in the closure of the document layer."

@keyed_value predicate
  args subject:text object:text
  closed true
  label en "keyed value"
  description "Document view: for a positive atom of a predicate declared with key N (a functional predicate), the predicate and its key argument as text, and the remaining arguments as text. Two different values under one key are a conflict."
